  "conclusions": [
    "Plain CpuU16 flags preserves all180 raw bodies and relocation targets exactly; VSUBC remains512 bytes with487 materialized differences from its480-byte original. This closes the previously missing native full-TU unsigned16 control.",
    "True signed64 operand subtraction with signed32 predicates emits592-byte VSUBC, including eight CDQ and four SBB instructions across the four expanded lanes. The original has none of these high-half operations. Positive/zero flag selection still lowers through SETLE.",
    "Combining unsigned16 flags with true signed64 subtraction emits the same VSUBC body as the wide-subtraction-only control. Neither width boundary restores the original three-way branch form.",
    "Every build preserves168/180 exact functions, all25 typed objects, all11 fields and zero unresolved relocations. The179 other raw function bodies and relocation destinations are unchanged; no extra helper function is emitted.",
    "Canonical RSP.cpp is unchanged. No candidate was promoted based on contribution size or positional difference count."
  ],
